    "result_text": "All tests green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`customerCode` is assigned on owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` plus a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`AssignCustomerCode` function** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility step: reads the built `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners via `OwnerRepository.findAll(Pageable)` (a COUNT query, reusing the existing repository method rather than loading all rows), and sets `customerCode = <LAST3>-<count+1>`. It mutates the owner in place before it is saved, consistent with `DefaultRegistrationDate`.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `save`, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema (like `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps `Owner.customerCode \u2192 OwnerDto.customerCode` (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`). No mapper edits needed.\n\n5. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table across all four DB scripts (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql).\n\nThe counting happens inside the create transaction before the save, so consecutive creates yield consecutive sequence numbers, which the acceptance test asserts. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nNote: the JDBC repository's `find*` SELECTs don't project the new column, but they already omit `email`/`registration_date` too, and the test/default profiles use `spring-data-jpa`, so I left that pre-existing pattern untouched to keep the change scoped.",
